    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "The patient was diagnosed by neurological symptoms of SMS. The paper lists the following criteria for SMS: (1) initial stiffness and rigidity in the axial muscles; (2) slow progression of stiffness to include proximal limb muscles, making volitional movements and ambulation difficult; (3) a fixed deformity of the spine, as in lordosis, and with some patients a restriction of hip movement; (4) the presence of superimposed episodic spasms precipitated by sudden movements, jarring noise, and emotional upset; (5) normal findings on motor and sensory nerve examinations; (6) normal intellect; and (7) electromyographic findings typical of continuous motor activity that can be abolished by intravenous or orally administered diazepam.",
      "quote": "We describe a patient diagnosed by neurological symptoms of SMS who also met criteria for generalized anxiety, major depression, and panic disorder.",
      "confidence": "high"
